Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 libspa-0.2-modules (>= ${sp9:PipeWireMin}),
 libspa-0.2-modules (<< ${sp9:PipeWireNext}),
Recommends: wireplumber (>= 0.5)
Description: patched libcamera 0.8.0 for the Surface Pro 9 cameras (experimental)
 libcamera 0.8.0 with the patches the two cameras of the Microsoft Surface Pro 9
 (Intel) need from the simple pipeline handler and its software ISP: no purple
 lines from the GPU debayer, metering over the visible image, stable exposure
 with the real sensor gain ranges, contrast detection autofocus for the rear
 camera, and a lens that is powered only while the camera streams.
 .
 It is installed in its own prefix, /usr/lib/sp9-libcamera, beside the
 distribution's libcamera, together with a build of PipeWire's libcamera SPA
 plugin (from PipeWire ${sp9:PipeWireVersion}) against it. Drop-ins for the
 pipewire and wireplumber user services put that plugin ahead of the
 distribution's, so PipeWire clients use the patched libcamera. Other
 libcamera users (GStreamer libcamerasrc, the distribution's cam) keep the
 distribution's libcamera. The package replaces no file.
 .
 The plugin must match the installed PipeWire release series; after a
 PipeWire upgrade to another series this package needs a rebuild.
